#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# haar_wavelet

#% text
# `haar_wavelet()` is the Haar wavelet, the orthonormal wavelet with the low-pass filter [1, 1]/sqrt(2). It is the default wavelet of the discrete transforms.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
d = discrete_wavelet_transform([1, 3, 5, 7], haar_wavelet(), 1)

#% cell
d(all)
#% output
#= [[0] -> [2.8284271247461903, 8.485281374238571], [1] -> [-1.4142135623730954, -1.414213562373095]]

#% text
# The approximation holds the scaled pairwise sums, the detail the scaled pairwise differences:

#% cell
chop(d(all)[1][2] - [4, 12]/sqrt(2.))
#% output
#= [0, 0]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `daubechies_wavelet`, `discrete_wavelet_transform`
